[{:seon.task/name "an-answer-pairs-by-request-and-stop-ends-a-wedged-server"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-25 by the stability sweep (docs/failure-points.md), checked against the code; split from `seon.fork-server/every-fork-server-wait-ends-with-the-server`, which answers a lost server's waits. (1) :stats and :static answers pair with :waiters by FIFO (`peek`). After a promote the standby is sent every unanswered request again, so FIFO holds only while every answer the dead server wrote arrived whole before its EOF; an answer cut by the death pairs the next waiter with the wrong request. The request carries its :rid to the server and the answer echoes it, and the proc answers the waiter by :rid. (2) `seon.fork-server/release!` waits for the boot server's exit with a blocking `c-waitpid` (no WNOHANG), so a wedged server (a deadlocked child, docs/failure-points.md#physics-who-may-run-threads) hangs root's stop; then `.join 5000` on the event reader is a clock deciding (§4). Stop is a kill of the server's process group (as a root's processes end with it, AGENTS.md §8) followed by the reap and the reader's EOF, and no timeout. Deletes the join's timeout; replaces FIFO pairing with :rid pairing."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.procs-test/a-promoted-servers-answers-pair-by-request-id seon.procs-test/stop-ends-a-wedged-fork-server}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-fork-servers-idle-wait-is-two-parks"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the blocking-calls audit of 2026-10-25 (docs/failure-points.md; row 25). What exists: the fork server waits for root and its children in one kqueue call, seon.lib/kq-wait (fork_server.clj:185), with no timeout and :blocking, so it is correct only while the server hosts no other fiber, and lib.clj kq-new/kq-watch/kq-wait and native/probe.c are kqueue only. Correct: root's socket is poller/wait-ready fd :read and a child exit is the poller child-exit wait (jolt.io-poller/a-fiber-waits-for-a-childs-exit); kq-new, kq-watch, kq-wait and the adopt path go. Needs seon.sock/a-send-parks-like-a-receive for its event sends. Proof to write: the server answers a frame while a child exit and a send are pending, on one carrier."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
